 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? A sketch is a quick drawing or plan, usually done very roughly, while a study is a more detailed drawing that an artist does before a final piece. Kind of, yes. lot of artists do lot of small studies before starting a big painting, so they know how everything fits together. Clouds are tough. Do you want to paint them from a photo, or try painting a few sky swatches next to each other and mixing them as you go? What looks wrong with the clouds? The lightness, the texture, or the shape? Good luck. Clouds are easy to overdo, so start with very loose strokes near the horizon and get thicker as you move up.",
